心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:30.820
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:30.820
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:30.820
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:38.510
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:38.510
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:38.510
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.770
Episode One:
     Welcome

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:00.230
But is that true?

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.220
Come over here!

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.360
Buenos tardes!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.770
The flight leaving for Foundation 2, Stellvia...

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.300
...will be departing on schedule.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.750
We will begin boarding shortly, so all passengers...

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:52.560
...please proceed to Gate Three.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:51.760
It's almost time, isn't it?

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:57.330
The flight leaving for Foundation 2, Stellvia will be departing on schedule.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:53.570
Yeah.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.700
Are you sure you don't want to wait for Masato and Chiaki?

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.200
We will begin boarding shortly, so all passengers...

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.530
I'm not going to wait.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.860
...please proceed to Gate Three.

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:00.780
The bad ones are the ones that overslept.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:11.440
Well, this might be a good time for Chiaki and you.

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:12.530
Hmm?

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:14.950
What do you mean, "good time"?

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.690
Leaving the nest, and letting one's children go.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.650
I'm fine!

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:22.800
Between the two of us, Chi-chan is the one with the problem!

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.380
What about this does she dislike so much?

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.960
I thought about this really hard before I decided, but even still...

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:33.180
Decide your own path by yourself...

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.700
Chiaki... your mother understands that...

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.370
It's just... that was very sudden for your mother.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.470
I thought that Chi-chan of all people would understand.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:51.830
Oh!

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.250
Sis!

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:54.960
Huh?

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.620
Good morning!

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:59.140
Masato? Why are you here?

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.330
So, how did that issue work out?

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:03.880
Huh?

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:04.650
Yeah!

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.370
A mother and sister who compete with each other...

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.240
...and as the younger brother who is worried about that...

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:11.580
I put forth a little effort!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:13.430
Huh?

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:34.290
You're late, Shima Katase!

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:37.700
What? What's this? Weren't you not going to come?

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:38.970
Of course I'm going to come!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.940
It's your departure, after all!

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:43.800
I came all the way to Peru from Japan...

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.940
...and paid the transportation fees to see you off!

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.770
Then why?

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.810
If you're going to argue with your parents, then run off.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:59.520
Don't go looking for kind words!

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.300
Even if we're far apart, I won't be sad!

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:17.040
I have Umihito! And I have Masato!

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:19.860
Listen up, you spoiled little daughter!

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.510
Don't come back until you've made something of yourself!

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:24.890
Hmph!

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.250
I WILL come back!

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.250
I'll make something of myself, and come back!

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:33.990
And when I do...

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:44.790
You really controlled yourself well.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.440
Do your best, Shima.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:04.450
The flight leaving for Foundation 2, Stellvia...

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.340
...will be departing on schedule.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.290
The flight leaving for Foundation 2, Stellvia...

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.650
...will be departing on schedule.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:14.720
Sis!

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.410
Buenos tardes!

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.360
We thank you very much for using...

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:53.230
...the Earth Public Corporation Gravity Transportation System...

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:55.370
...for your travels.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:55.320
Oh, that's right!

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:56.560
Here.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:57.310
Huh?

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:58.590
A farewell gift.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:02.550
Thank you...

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.050
Be sure to eat it with care!

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:15.760
Hmm...

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:32.800
Wow!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.350
And what is that?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:35.790
Huh?

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.860
Er, um, it's called "compeito".

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.150
It's a cute little confection, isn't it?

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.470
Oh, wo-would you like to eat some?

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.290
Oh, no, be sure to cherish that.

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:52.900
Right...

00:08:55.430 --> 00:08:59.530
The Nasca flight departing for Stellvia will be taking off shortly.

00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:01.780
Please take your seats immediately.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:07.510
The Nasca flight departing for Stellvia will be taking off shortly.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.270
Please take your seats immediately.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.430
Whoa!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.540
The arm has detached!

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:29.830
At times during takeoff, the video will become considerably unstable.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:33.560
This is due to the influence of the gravity control.

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:37.570
Please understand that there is no problem with the safety of the ship.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.570
We will be taking off shortly.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:48.770
Whoa!

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:49.920
Wait, wait!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.850
My bad, it was my bad!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:01.860
I overslept.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:05.040
We will now be taking off.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.080
Incredible...

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:54.740
Shima-chan...

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:28.620
From now on, I'm going to walk looking upwards.

00:11:30.430 --> 00:11:32.060
Be sure to watch your feet.

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:04.040
The gravity jump occurred without any problems.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:06.070
For the next three hours and thirty minutes...

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:08.120
...please enjoy your trip through the sky.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:13.500
But seriously, it just doesn't jump out at you!

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:20.230
They say we're in space, but we can't see outside, you know?

00:12:20.300 --> 00:12:21.500
R-right...

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:25.140
And of course, you're another person going to the Space Academy, right?

00:12:25.690 --> 00:12:26.730
Y-yeah.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.830
Actually, everyone that's going to the Foundation...

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.540
...is either a new student or is involved with a store.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.840
What about you, mister?

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.020
Hmm.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:37.990
Why don't you try and guess?

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:39.680
So that's how it's going to be.

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:41.050
Then it's that!

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.850
You're the owner of a coffee shop...

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:45.000
...or someone who's going to sell fried chicken at a store, right?

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:47.290
That's rich.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.090
And what's your name?

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:50.790
What?

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:53.150
I'm Arisa Glennorth!

00:12:54.360 --> 00:12:55.300
Um...

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:58.310
...my name is Shima Katase.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:01.000
"My name is" makes us sound like strangers.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.180
Let's be friendly, okay?

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.470
Right.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:06.160
Drop the "My name is" and try once more!

00:13:06.420 --> 00:13:08.380
I'm Shima Katase.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.810
Oh, so you've flown in high altitude before.

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.160
Yeah, in summer camp.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:27.140
Wow, that's incredible.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:28.060
What about you?

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:29.210
Well, I...

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:33.050
Here you are.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:35.580
Hmm.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.080
Is this really all right?

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:39.390
Oh, no, I'm going to eat some, too, so...

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:42.920
This one is sugar flavor.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:44.900
Maple flavor.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:46.450
And this one?

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.080
It's soda flavor.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.330
What are you planning on doing when you get to the Stellvia?

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:11.880
Well, I guess I'll study...

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:14.140
Of course you'll study...

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.750
The question is, what will you do after you've studied?

00:14:18.100 --> 00:14:20.780
For what reason are you studying?

00:14:22.510 --> 00:14:25.110
In any case, I wanted to go into outer space.

00:14:25.570 --> 00:14:26.140
Oh...

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:28.820
Not look up at it, but look at it normally.

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:31.760
How can I put this from the center, and straight ahead!

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:35.070
Outer space from straight ahead, huh?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:38.330
You say some pretty philosophical things, don't you?

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:42.280
I've often been called strange.

00:14:42.410 --> 00:14:43.080
Oh...

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.900
That's why this is so amazing.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.110
I thought that it was incredible...

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.000
...that I passed the Space Academy interview exam.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:52.390
I was on top of the world, and happy, so happy.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.030
I thought that I was lucky...

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:05.050
U-um...

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.140
Sleeping complete!

00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:18.120
Captain, there's a message from the Stellvia.

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:19.640
Put it through.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:22.310
This is the Stellvia.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:25.550
Are there any changes to the Fujiyama's arrival schedule?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.620
This is FJ101, the Fujiyama.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.320
No problems, we're right on schedule.

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:32.070
Roger that.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:33.590
Look forward to the show!

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:34.990
Well, then.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.330
I heard that it'll be really extravagant this year.

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.560
Mmm, I'm looking forward to it.

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.410
We will be able to see Foundation 2, the Stellvia very soon.

00:15:48.360 --> 00:15:50.280
Our current speed is 3,000 kilometers.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.000
It's the Stellvia!

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:30.750
Where is it?

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:32.350
Look, over there!

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:54.970
That's...

00:16:55.590 --> 00:16:56.620
...the Stellvia.

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:57.680
Yeah...

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.610
The Stellvia.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:08.020
We have made eye contact with the Fujiyama.

00:17:08.390 --> 00:17:09.450
It's right on time.

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.190
Ayaka, for now, say hello.

00:17:11.410 --> 00:17:12.020
Roger.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:13.180
Leave it to me.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:18.820
Right now, in the year 2356...

00:17:19.480 --> 00:17:21.550
...we are going to begin the welcoming party...

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.790
...for the new students to the Space Academy Stellvia!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:25.640
Welcoming Party

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:34.140
Now, let's begin.

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.870
All units, launch!

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:10.810
We're going to finish this in one shot.

00:18:10.890 --> 00:18:11.450
Go!

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:26.990
There they are!

00:18:40.640 --> 00:18:44.710
This is the general leader, Ayaka Machida, of the second term class.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.770
New students, welcome to the Stellvia!

00:18:51.060 --> 00:18:53.750
We welcome you!

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:57.350
I feel like Peter Pan.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:02.040
Outside my window is Tinkerbell.

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:04.330
And next to me is...

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.430
What?

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.830
And next to me is Wendy.

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:18.330
Do you think that we'll be able to fly like that?

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:24.850
Katase, let's be friends.

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:25.510
What?

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:28.250
I want to be...

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:30.960
...friends with you.

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:36.710
No?

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:40.990
Sure, that's fine.

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:53.040
The journey to the stars is a long one...

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:56.790
The Ora-avis Machine, Katie.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.080
I wonder how many years from now it will be until you pilot them...

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.560
It seems you really don't remember.

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:07.940
Examinee number B3048!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:08.650
Hmm?

00:20:10.940 --> 00:20:11.630
You!

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:13.410
You're the one from the interview exam!

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:17.530
Enter, Shima Katase.

00:20:23.000 --> 00:20:23.700
What!?

00:20:24.520 --> 00:20:26.310
You're not the owner of a coffee shop!?

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:31.750
I'm Richard James, chairman of the Space Academy Stellvia.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:36.960
Welcome to the Stellvia.

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:45.000
How was the Earth?

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:47.490
I was able to meet some excellent people.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.210
Although they pushed this on me.

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.420
That was a great welcome party, wasn't it?

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:02.280
Yeah.

00:21:05.390 --> 00:21:07.990
Nice to meet you, honorable roommate.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:11.310
Same here, nice to meet you.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.010
Welcoming Party

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:27.890
Good work on the welcoming flight.

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:30.380
Good work to you too, head of the implementation committee.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:35.270
To be shown something like that first, the new students sure are lucky.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:39.680
If they admire it, get encouraged by it, then study...

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:43.560
If that happens, then there might be more competitors for you.

00:21:43.960 --> 00:21:46.870
At that time, I won't hold back, and I'll crush them.

00:21:55.090 --> 00:22:00.620
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.090 --> 00:22:00.620
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.090 --> 00:22:00.620
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:07.300
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:07.300
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:07.300
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:15.060
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:15.060
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:15.060
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:20.970
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:20.970
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.190 --> 00:22:20.970
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:28.750
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:28.750
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:28.750
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:35.670
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:35.670
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.340 --> 00:22:35.670
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:42.460
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:42.460
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:36.020 --> 00:22:42.460
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:51.630
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:51.630
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:51.630
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:58.680
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:58.680
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.240 --> 00:22:58.680
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:04.590
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:04.590
And still I looked up

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:04.590
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

